Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:05:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Newton solver: stagnation criterion fixed after an
 independent review

- The stagnation is detected over a window: the residual has not
  decreased by more than 10 % during the last two iterations (the window
  starts again otherwise). The previous version compared each iteration
  with the smallest residual, so that two iterations with a factor 0.6
  were accepted. A slow convergence, even with a factor 0.9 per
  iteration, is not taken for a stagnation: this matters since the
  relative tolerance applies to the reference residual, which is the one
  of the prediction, if any, much larger than the residuals of the
  resolution.
- The residual at the floor is noisy (from 615 to 7594 on a step of the
  finite strain test in float): the best iterate of the resolution is
  kept, the behaviours being integrated again at this iterate, instead of
  the last one.
- No convergence order is printed after a stagnation.
- UniaxialTensileTest-Stagnation-IsotropicLinearHardeningPlasticity is
  removed: it converged without the criterion. The finite strain tests
  check the messages (the stagnation accepted, or the resolution failed),
  and the failure prints the error message of the context.
- Configuration check of hypre: cmake_push_check_state; the Gaussian
  eliminations 98 and 198 and AME are also affected.
- Documentation: the tolerance is relative to the reference residual, the
  floors measured in finite strain (3e-4 to 8e-4 on a cube of one
  element), a glossary entry, and the FixedPoint solver without this
  criterion.

Float suite: 223/223 (91 stagnations accepted, 53 best iterates
restored). Double: CI simulation 208/208, examples 22/22, mm-opera-hpc
6/6 with the same results bit for bit, no stagnation in the logs.
